@nsobid-FF773E90972D544EB79406EAA65396D53C43EFB9

# Super Mario Bros. Wonder [010015100B514000] v1.2.1 - 4:3 Aspect Ratio + HUD un-stretch (RomCore)
# Plain 4:3 camera lines first, then two code hooks (code cave in the zero padding at the end of .text, 0x2138650+):
#  1) Layout::Build override epilogue (0x61C9C): for every ui2d layout whose root pane is >= 500 tall (full-screen layouts;
#     nested parts layouts are skipped) squash the root pane Y scale to 0.75 (the host later stretches the 16:9 buffer by 4/3,
#     so the HUD ends up undistorted), and enlarge big panes (height 0.9x..1.35x of the root, not full-width Capture panes)
#     by 4/3 so full-height backgrounds still cover the 4:3 screen.
#  2) Pane::CalculateMtx (0x10A8BBC): after the pane's local Y (origin alignment included) is known, a pane whose world
#     centre sits between 0.15H and 0.465H away from the layout centre while its parent is still inside 0.15H is moved
#     outwards by H/6 (H = root height, 1080 by default) so top/bottom anchored HUD stays glued to the real screen edges.

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

@enabled
02AEEDB4 ABAAAA3F
02AEE9E8 5555A541
02AEEBD8 5555A5C1
02AEE968 55552541
02AEE834 555525C1
02138650  // Build hook: root squash
00061C9C 6D5A8314 // b 0x2138650
02138774  // CalculateMtx hook: edge anchor
010A8BBC EE3E4214 // b 0x2138774
@stop
